  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">QuantaPep v4.0 is still early in its public life, but the record already shows a small trace of uptake: 11 downloads, 163 views, and one documented downstream reuse. At present, the scholarly citation count remains at zero, so the clearest evidence of reach comes from repository usage and the linked reuse signal rather than citation-based influence.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Zenodo preprint introduces an autonomous, genotype-aware platform for peptide discovery, positioning the work at the intersection of computational biology, machine learning, and drug discovery. The abstract frames the contribution around a practical bottleneck in therapeutic peptide design: existing pipelines are difficult to scale across human genetic diversity and often rely on fragmented validation steps. In response, the article presents QuantaPep v4.0 as a closed-loop system that combines sequence design, structural validation, and manufacturing-aware optimization.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In terms of attention, the measurable footprint is modest but real. The repository record shows 163 views and 11 downloads, suggesting that the item has been discovered and sampled by readers, even though the available citation landscape is not yet developed. OpenAlex currently records no citations, so the article\u2019s scholarly impact should be read as emerging rather than established.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A more distinctive signal is reuse: the metadata documents one downstream reuse event, classified as an associated article. That indicates the work has already been incorporated into a connected scholarly record, which is a stronger sign of uptake than passive viewing alone. The stewardship record also shows that the preprint is hosted in Zenodo, an open repository with persistent DOI infrastructure and open access availability in the repository network.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the article\u2019s impact profile is best characterized as an early-stage, infrastructure-backed contribution with preliminary signs of engagement and reuse. The record supports interest in the platform and its method rather than mature citation impact. Because public discourse, scite counts, and citation evidence are sparse or absent in the available sources, the strongest story here is about availability, discoverability, and first reuse rather than broad external adoption.</p>",
